### Description

```
      const { embedding: query } = await embed({  
        model: vertex.textEmbeddingModel('gemini-embedding-001'),  
        value: 'Before the arrival of Chili Peppers from the Americas, Indians relied on less intense heat from long peppers, black peppers, and other ingredients', 
        providerOptions: {  
          google: {  
            taskType: 'RETRIEVAL_QUERY',  
          },  
        },  
      });
```

The `taskType` parameter is silently ignored by the google vertex embeddings api because it expects fields inside of `instances` to be snake case

Solution:
Have the AI SDK pass the snake case parameter internally. Externally, the DX remains the same as does the documentation.

[Source](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/model-reference/text-embeddings-api)

